  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe utilizes 2 (2-compartment) food storage containers.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a grill pan, outdoor grill, or regular skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the pan heats up, pat the chicken dry with paper towels. Holding a knife parallel to the cutting board, cut the chicken in half horizontally to form thin fillets. Season both sides with salt and pepper.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ lb chicken breasts, boneless skinless\n¼ tsp salt\n⅛ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the pan is hot, coat with oil. Add chicken and grill, flipping once, until golden and cooked through, 8-10 minutes. Remove to a plate. (Reserve pan for later use.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tsp extra virgin olive oil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, wash and dry the fresh produce. (Skip the spinach if it came pre-washed.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ English cucumber\n1 tomato\n¼ (5 oz) pkg baby spinach"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Using a clean cutting board, trim and halve cucumber lengthwise, then cut crosswise into thin half-moons. Halve tomato lengthwise, then cut into ½-inch thick wedges. Divide both between one of the compartments in each storage container, then drizzle with balsamic glaze and set aside. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tbsp balsamic glaze"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Slice grilled chicken into strips.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place tortillas on a flat surface, then top with grilled chicken, spinach, and cheese. Drizzle with ranch dressing, then roll tightly to close. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup mozzarella cheese, shredded\n3 tbsp ranch dressing"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Return the pan to medium-high heat. Add wraps and grill, turning occasionally, until tortillas are crispy and golden. Remove from heat, cut in half, and set aside to cool, about 10 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add cooled wraps to the other compartment of the storage containers, cover, and refrigerate until ready to eat. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
